$ nexoctl admin kms status mem
KMS: builtin (online)
Default key: mem-kms-key

$ nexoctl admin kms key ls mem
KEY                              CREATED                 DEFAULT
mem-kms-key                      -                       yes

$ nexoctl admin kms key create mem app-key
Created the KMS key "app-key".

$ nexoctl admin kms key create mem app-key
! nexoctl: error: create KMS key "app-key": kms key app-key already exists (conflict)
[exit 1]

$ nexoctl admin kms key ls --json mem app
{"status":"success","alias":"mem","id":"app-key","createdAt":"2026-01-02T03:04:05Z"}

$ nexoctl admin kms reseal mem
Re-sealed 3 of 3 data keys (3 versions, 0 pending uploads) in 2 buckets.

$ nexoctl admin kms reseal --json mem --bucket docs
{"status":"success","alias":"mem","bucket":"docs","buckets":2,"versions":3,"uploads":0,"resealed":3,"failed":0}

$ nexoctl admin kms reseal mem
Re-sealed 1 of 2 data keys (2 versions, 0 pending uploads) in 1 bucket. 1 failed, first: docs/a.txt: kms: key not found
! nexoctl: error: 1 data key could not be re-sealed
[exit 1]

$ nexoctl encrypt set sse-kms app-key mem/docs
Default encryption of `mem/docs`: SSE-KMS with key app-key.

$ nexoctl encrypt info mem/docs
`mem/docs`: SSE-KMS with key app-key.

$ nexoctl encrypt set sse-s3 app-key mem/docs
! nexoctl: error: a KEY needs sse-kms: encrypt set sse-kms KEY ALIAS/BUCKET
! Run 'nexoctl encrypt set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl encrypt set sse-kms app-key --kms-key-id other mem/docs
! nexoctl: error: give the KMS key once: as KEY or with --kms-key-id
! Run 'nexoctl encrypt set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl quota set mem/docs --size 1MiB
Set a hard quota of 1.0MiB on `mem/docs`.

$ nexoctl quota info mem/docs
`mem/docs` has a hard quota of 1.0MiB (used 768.0KiB in 3 objects, 75.0%).

$ nexoctl quota info --json mem/docs
{"status":"success","target":"mem/docs","bucket":"docs","type":"hard","size":1048576,"used":786432,"objects":3}

$ nexoctl admin kms status mem
! nexoctl: error: server side encryption specified but KMS is not configured (not_implemented)
[exit 1]

